  "member_id": "wahren-herlenius-marie",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/medicine_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B007",
        "laureates": [
          "Marc Feldmann",
          "Ravinder N. Maini"
        ],
        "citation": "for establishing TNF blockade as a treatment for rheumatoid arthritis and inflammatory disease"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B024",
    "B001"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B007 remains the most balanced case across mechanistic insight, direct and durable patient benefit, historical maturity, and creditability. It converted a pathogenic TNF hypothesis into decisive clinical evidence, transformed rheumatoid arthritis treatment, and established a therapeutic principle with sustained consequences across inflammatory disease. Feldmann and Maini provide a focused attribution for the central mechanistic and clinical demonstration, provided the citation is confined to that foundational principle rather than subsequent development of individual anti-TNF agents.",
    "case_against": "The development, optimization, and evaluation of specific anti-TNF medicines involved substantial further academic, industrial, and clinical contributions. B007 therefore cannot be presented as crediting all later drug development. B024 has broader metabolic reach and B001 offers a more foundational cellular framework, so the comparative judgment depends on giving real weight both to explanatory scope and to direct clinical causal proof.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "linnarsson-sten",
        "point": "Linnarsson ranked B024 first because GLP-1 physiology combines fundamental endocrine biology with major, mature therapeutic consequences in diabetes and obesity, while recognizing uncertainty about separating foundational work from later pharmaceutical optimization.",
        "response": "I agree that B024 is an exceptional achievement with profound clinical consequences and remains my leading therapeutic alternative. Its attribution boundary is nevertheless materially broader: peptide discovery, receptor biology, medicinal optimization, and drug development are difficult to separate under a three-person cap. B007 has a more compact link from a defined inflammatory mechanism to clinical testing of the therapeutic principle, with a longer and clearly bounded record across inflammatory diseases."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "perlmann-thomas",
        "point": "Perlmann ranked B001 first, emphasizing the unfolded protein response as a fundamental, mature, and broadly explanatory cellular framework with a focused Mori-Walter attribution.",
        "response": "I agree that B001 is an unusually strong fundamental-science configuration and that its attribution is comparatively clear. I retain B007 because it supplies not only a mechanistic insight but a long, direct test of that insight in patients, with durable therapeutic consequences. This gives direct clinical transformation substantial weight without reducing the value of foundational biology to immediate application."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "sandberg-rickard",
        "point": "Sandberg ranked B008 first for its narrowly defined splicing mechanism and decisive therapeutic benefit in spinal muscular atrophy, while questioning whether the Krainer-Bennett pair captures all indispensable contributions.",
        "response": "The chair's distinction is important: B008 can be valued as a bounded SMA achievement without claiming that antisense medicine is generally established by it. Even on that bounded basis, I retain B007 because its clinical and historical record is longer and the Feldmann-Maini attribution more cleanly connects the central hypothesis with its clinical validation."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether historical review can delimit Feldmann and Maini's foundational therapeutic principle and clinical demonstration sufficiently from later anti-TNF drug development.",
      "How the relative weight of B007's direct, mature clinical transformation should compare with B001's broader foundational explanatory reach and B024's broader metabolic consequences.",
      "Whether a more complete account of the central anti-TNF clinical demonstration would identify indispensable contributors beyond the proposed pair."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "My research background includes autoimmunity and rheumatology, but the supplied profile documents no collaboration or other connection with Marc Feldmann or Ravinder N. Maini. I disclose the field proximity; no recusal basis is apparent from the supplied evidence."
  }
}
